# Add --dry-run to Cancel Command

## Problem
`rch cancel --all` immediately cancels all builds. Users may want to preview what would be cancelled before committing.

## Current Behavior
```bash
$ rch cancel --all
Cancelled 5 builds.  # Immediate, no preview
```

## Proposed Behavior
```bash
$ rch cancel --all --dry-run
Would cancel 5 builds:
  b-1234  cargo build --release   [worker: css, 2m 15s]
  b-1235  cargo test              [worker: csd, 45s]
  b-1236  cargo clippy            [worker: css, 1m 30s]
  b-1237  cargo build             [worker: cse, 3m 02s]
  b-1238  bun typecheck           [worker: csd, 12s]

Run without --dry-run to cancel.
```

## Implementation
```rust
async fn cancel_builds(all: bool, build_id: Option<u64>, dry_run: bool) -> Result<()> {
    let builds = if all {
        get_all_active_builds().await?
    } else {
        vec\![get_build(build_id.unwrap()).await?]
    };

    if dry_run {
        println\!("Would cancel {} builds:", builds.len());
        for build in &builds {
            println\!("  {}  {}  [worker: {}, {}]",
                build.id, build.command, build.worker, build.elapsed);
        }
        println\!("\nRun without --dry-run to cancel.");
        return Ok(());
    }

    // Actual cancellation
}
```

