## Task
Implement concurrent querying of all workers with proper timeout handling.

## What to Implement
Replace sequential fake status with parallel real queries:

\`\`\`rust
// Before (stub):
Ok(workers.iter().map(|w| WorkerStatus {
    worker_id: w.id.0.clone(),
    reachable: true,   // Always true! NEVER ACTUALLY CHECKED
    healthy: true,     // Always true!
    version: Some("0.1.0".into()),  // HARDCODED!
    issues: vec![],
}).collect())

// After (real):
use futures::stream::{self, StreamExt};

const MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES: usize = 10;
const DEFAULT_QUERY_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(10);

pub async fn get_fleet_status(
    workers: &[&WorkerConfig],  // NOTE: slice of references in actual signature
    ctx: &OutputContext,
) -> Result<Vec<WorkerStatus>> {
    if workers.is_empty() {
        tracing::debug!("No workers to query");
        return Ok(vec![]);
    }

    tracing::info!(count = %workers.len(), "Starting fleet status query");

    if !ctx.is_json() {
        eprintln!("Querying {} workers...", workers.len());
    }

    let start = std::time::Instant::now();

    // Query all workers in parallel with bounded concurrency
    let results: Vec<WorkerStatus> = stream::iter(workers)
        .map(|worker| query_single_worker(*worker, DEFAULT_QUERY_TIMEOUT))
        .buffer_unordered(MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES)
        .collect()
        .await;

    // Log summary
    let reachable_count = results.iter().filter(|r| r.reachable).count();
    let healthy_count = results.iter().filter(|r| r.healthy).count();
    let unreachable_count = results.len() - reachable_count;

    tracing::info!(
        total = %results.len(),
        reachable = %reachable_count,
        healthy = %healthy_count,
        unreachable = %unreachable_count,
        duration_ms = %start.elapsed().as_millis(),
        "Fleet status query complete"
    );

    if !ctx.is_json() && unreachable_count > 0 {
        eprintln!("Warning: {} worker(s) unreachable", unreachable_count);
    }

    Ok(results)
}
\`\`\`

## Technical Details

### Bounded Concurrency
- Use \`buffer_unordered\` for parallel execution with max concurrency
- MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES = 10 (configurable constant)
- Prevents overwhelming network or SSH agent with too many connections

### Per-Worker Timeout
- Each query has individual timeout (DEFAULT_QUERY_TIMEOUT = 10s)
- Timed-out workers return with reachable=false
- Use tokio::time::timeout wrapper inside query_single_worker

### Empty Workers Handling
- Return empty vec immediately if no workers provided
- Log at debug level

### Progress Reporting (Human Mode)
- Print "Querying N workers..." to stderr
- Print warning if any unreachable

