## Overview
Implement end-to-end tests that verify the complete self-test workflow: binary hash computation, code change, remote compilation, and hash verification.

## Background and Justification
The self-test infrastructure proves that RCH works correctly by compiling its own codebase. E2E tests must verify:
- Binary hashes are computed correctly
- Changes produce different binaries
- Compilation actually happens on workers
- Results are correctly transferred back
- Hash comparison detects differences

## Test Scenarios

### 1. Binary Hash Computation E2E
```rust
#[tokio::test]
async fn test_binary_hash_computation() {
    let harness = TestHarness::new("hash_computation").await;

    // Build the binary locally first
    harness.run_local_build("cargo build --release -p rch").await.unwrap();

    // Compute hash
    let binary_path = harness.project_root().join("target/release/rch");
    let hash = compute_sha256(&binary_path).await.unwrap();

    // Verify hash format
    assert_eq!(hash.len(), 64);  // SHA256 in hex
    assert!(hash.chars().all(|c| c.is_ascii_hexdigit()));

    // Verify determinism
    let hash2 = compute_sha256(&binary_path).await.unwrap();
    assert_eq!(hash, hash2);

    harness.cleanup().await;
}
```

### 2. Code Change Detection E2E
```rust
#[tokio::test]
async fn test_code_change_produces_different_hash() {
    let harness = TestHarness::new("code_change").await;

    // Initial build
    harness.run_local_build("cargo build --release -p rch").await.unwrap();
    let initial_hash = compute_binary_hash(&harness, "rch").await;

    // Make a code change (add a comment with timestamp)
    let main_rs = harness.project_root().join("rch/src/main.rs");
    let content = fs::read_to_string(&main_rs).await.unwrap();
    let modified = format!("// Build timestamp: {}\n{}", Utc::now(), content);
    fs::write(&main_rs, modified).await.unwrap();

    // Rebuild
    harness.run_local_build("cargo build --release -p rch").await.unwrap();
    let new_hash = compute_binary_hash(&harness, "rch").await;

    // Hashes should differ
    assert_ne!(initial_hash, new_hash);

    // Restore original
    fs::write(&main_rs, content).await.unwrap();
    harness.cleanup().await;
}
```

