## Edge Cases

- `package.json` exists but no lockfile: install proceeds with `npm install` (creates package-lock.json), warning logged
- `bun.lockb` is binary so blake3 hashing it works fine; no special handling
- `node_modules/.cache/` is large but is excluded from transfer (covered by existing exclusion patterns from rch-0w4)
- Worker has no `bun` binary installed: prepare returns Failed with clear error message + remediation suggestion (`apt install bun` or `curl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash`)
- Concurrent `prepare()` calls for the same project on the same worker: file-locked via the existing project-directory lease pattern in rch-wkr (do NOT introduce a new lock; reuse)
- Massive `node_modules` (>500MB): prepare's bytes_added metric flags it; user is informed without blocking
- `package.json` mentions optional native deps that fail to compile: install logs are preserved; surfaces clearly in the build report
- Hook context: `prepare` runs only on the worker side, never in the hook process — no impact on hook latency budget

