## Problem
Users cannot temporarily exclude a worker without editing config files:
- Worker is being maintained but not fully offline
- Worker is performing poorly and needs investigation
- User wants to test with specific workers only
- Worker is reserved for another team member

Current options are all-or-nothing:
- Remove from config (loses settings)
- Stop SSH (worker appears offline/errored)

## Solution
Add soft disable/enable for workers that persists in daemon state.

### CLI: rch workers disable/enable
```
$ rch workers list
ID            STATUS    SLOTS   SPEEDSCORE
gpu-server-1  healthy   16/16   187.3
cpu-server-2  healthy   8/8     92.4
laptop-dev    healthy   4/4     67.2

$ rch workers disable gpu-server-1 --reason="Maintenance window"
Worker gpu-server-1 disabled.
  Reason: Maintenance window
  Active builds: 2 (will complete, no new builds assigned)

$ rch workers list
ID            STATUS      SLOTS   SPEEDSCORE
gpu-server-1  disabled    14/16   187.3      ← Maintenance window
cpu-server-2  healthy     8/8     92.4
laptop-dev    healthy     4/4     67.2

# After maintenance
$ rch workers enable gpu-server-1
Worker gpu-server-1 enabled.
```

### Drain Mode
For graceful maintenance, drain existing builds before disabling:
```
$ rch workers disable gpu-server-1 --drain
Draining gpu-server-1...
  Waiting for 2 active builds to complete...
  [=====>    ] 1/2 complete
  [==========] 2/2 complete
Worker gpu-server-1 disabled (drained).
```

