## Overview
Implement disk I/O metrics collection for worker telemetry, reading from /proc/diskstats and /proc/sys/fs/file-nr to track I/O throughput, latency indicators, and file descriptor usage.

## Background and Justification
Disk I/O is often the bottleneck for compilation workloads. Rust compilation involves:
- Reading many source files and dependency crates
- Writing incremental compilation artifacts
- Building the final binary

Workers with saturated disk I/O should be deprioritized in worker selection.

## Implementation Details

### Data Sources (Linux)
```rust
// Read from /proc/diskstats
// Format: major minor name rd_io rd_merge rd_sect rd_tick wr_io wr_merge wr_sect wr_tick io_in_prog io_tick io_wtick

pub struct DiskStats {
    pub device: String,
    pub reads_completed: u64,
    pub reads_merged: u64,
    pub sectors_read: u64,
    pub time_reading_ms: u64,
    pub writes_completed: u64,
    pub writes_merged: u64,
    pub sectors_written: u64,
    pub time_writing_ms: u64,
    pub io_in_progress: u64,
    pub time_io_ms: u64,
    pub weighted_time_io_ms: u64,
}

// Calculate derived metrics
pub struct DiskMetrics {
    pub read_throughput_mbps: f64,
    pub write_throughput_mbps: f64,
    pub io_utilization_pct: f64,  // time_io_ms delta / elapsed_ms * 100
    pub avg_queue_depth: f64,     // weighted_time_io_ms delta / time_io_ms delta
    pub read_latency_ms: f64,     // time_reading_ms delta / reads_completed delta
    pub write_latency_ms: f64,    // time_writing_ms delta / writes_completed delta
}
```

### File Descriptor Tracking
```rust
// Read from /proc/sys/fs/file-nr
// Format: allocated_fds  free_fds  max_fds
// Example: 1234  0  9223372036854775807

pub struct FileDescriptorStats {
    pub allocated: u64,
    pub max: u64,
    pub used_pct: f64,  // allocated / max * 100
}
```

### Sampling Strategy
- Sample /proc/diskstats every 1 second
- Calculate deltas between samples for rate metrics
- Filter to relevant block devices (exclude loop, ram)
- Aggregate across all physical devices or report primary device

