## Problem
When workers become unhealthy or offline, users only discover this when:
- A build fails
- They manually run `rch workers list`
- They check the web dashboard

There is no proactive notification of worker issues.

## Solution
Add configurable alerting for worker health events.

### Alert Triggers
| Event | Default | Configurable |
|-------|---------|--------------|
| Worker goes offline | Alert | Yes |
| Worker becomes unhealthy | Alert | Yes |
| All workers offline | Critical Alert | No (always) |
| Worker CPU > threshold | Alert | Yes (default 90%) |
| Worker memory > threshold | Alert | Yes (default 90%) |
| Build failure rate > threshold | Alert | Yes (default 20%) |
| Self-test failure | Critical Alert | No (always) |
| Circuit breaker opens | Alert | Yes |

### Alert Channels

#### 1. CLI Notifications
```
$ rch status
⚠️  ALERT: Worker gpu-server-1 went offline 5 minutes ago
⚠️  ALERT: Worker cpu-server-2 CPU at 95% for 10 minutes

Workers: 1/3 healthy
```

#### 2. Desktop Notifications (Optional)
```toml
[alerts]
desktop_notifications = true
```
Uses `notify-rust` crate for cross-platform notifications.

#### 3. Webhook Integration
```toml
[alerts.webhook]
url = "https://hooks.slack.com/services/..."
# or
url = "https://discord.com/api/webhooks/..."
```

